  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Partial rotary is the detail people miss",
      "text": "With rope_freq_dim {{cfg.rope_inv_freq_len}}, only 2 · 3 · 16 = 96 of each head's {{cfg.attention_head_dim}} channels carry position; the remaining 32 are position-free. Wan rotates the entire head. If you port a RoPE trick between the two, this is what bites.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "mmx.dit",
          "lines": [
            427,
            431
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "MiniMaxH3Transformer3DModel",
            "first": "The number of rotary frequencies per axis. The `(t, h, w)` axes share one `inv_freq` buffer of this length",
            "sha": "c5cd65a5",
            "span": [
              384,
              770
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Both heads run over every row",
      "text": "proj_out and audio_proj_out are applied to the WHOLE sequence and only then index_select their modality's rows. Wasteful on paper, but it keeps the kernels dense and avoids a gather inside the block stack.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "call_site",
          "src": "mmx.dit",
          "lines": [
            761,
            763
